            "title": "Second tanker to skip fuel loading at sanctions-hit Nayara, sources say",
            "description": "",
            "summary": "SINGAPORE/NEW DELHI (Reuters) -A tanker will not load fuel from India's sanctions-hit Nayara Energy refinery as scheduled, according to three industry sources and LSEG shiptracking data, becoming the second such vessel to change plans following the European Union measures.  Nayara Energy, in which Russia's largest oil producer Rosneft has a 49.13% stake, was hit in a fresh package of sanctions imposed on Friday by the European Union over Russia's war on Ukraine that began in February 2022.  The Chang Hang Xing Yun is now tentatively set to load about 35,000 metric tons (260,750 barrels) of ultra-low sulphur diesel (ULSD) from Kuwait on August 1 before heading to East Africa, according to data from LSEG shiptracking and a shipping source on Wednesday.",
